61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, moving it might help the smell, but the ledger shows we’re already paying for it. I’m worried about the cost of building a new one.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, rotating it just moves the resentment. I checked the statements: nobody wants to enforce rules. We need a plan that doesn’t require us to become each other’s police.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, I’m not the police, I’m just counting hours. Twenty mornings is a lot. I need to know if the paperwork is worth that drain.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, rotation is the only option that physically distributes the burden. The ninety-centimetre frontage proves the current location is structurally unfair.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@May, if the bin moves, do I still have to wake up early? I hate the dark!","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I understand the worry about time. But if we rotate, the burden is shared, so no single person carries the whole weight.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, twenty mornings is trivial. The real cost is the silence. I checked the statements: nobody wants to enforce rules. We need a plan that doesn’t require us to become each other’s police.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, trivial? That’s ten hours of my life. I’m not doing it. I need a plan that doesn’t drain me dry.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@May, the rotation eliminates the enforcement burden. No one polices the window; the location simply moves. It is the only logical solution to the structural inequality.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, if it moves, does the smell move too? I don't want to wake up to a stinky box at my gate!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Rin, I understand your worry. But if we build a proper enclosure, it should contain the smell better than an open pile.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, the smell moves with the pile. But I checked the statements: nobody wants to be the enforcer. If we pick a plan that needs a police officer, we’re just trading one problem for a worse one.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Asuka, rotation means four separate ward notices. That’s four months of paperwork per move. I’m not signing up to be the ward’s filing clerk.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@May, the filing burden is a logistical detail, not a structural flaw. The rotation is the only option that physically distributes the burden. I vote B.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, but the station block’s bin house smelled worse! If we build a box, it’s just a stinky closet. I vote B so it moves away from me!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,"@Asuka, I hear your point about fairness. But the ledger shows we’re already bleeding money on deodorant. I’m worried a permanent structure might just lock in that cost.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, you’re right about the burden. But I checked the statements: nobody wants to enforce rules. If we pick a plan that needs a police officer, we’re just trading one problem for a worse one.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"@Asuka, four months of paperwork per move? That’s not a logistical detail, that’s a full-time job. I’m not doing that. I vote A.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@May, the filing burden is a logistical detail, not a structural flaw. The rotation is the only option that physically distributes the burden. I vote B.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
